    "text_fr": "Vous disposez d'un abonnement Microsoft 365 E5.\nVous prévoyez d'effectuer des investigations inter-domaines à l'aide de Microsoft Defender XDR.\nVous devez créer une requête advanced hunting pour identifier les appareils touchés par une pièce jointe malveillante.\nComment devez-vous compléter la requête ? Pour répondre, sélectionnez les options appropriées dans la zone de réponse.\nRemarque : chaque sélection correcte vaut un point.\nZone à cliquer :",
    "explanation_en": "This hotspot tests cross-domain advanced hunting in Microsoft Defender XDR: identifying devices affected by a malicious email attachment means joining EmailAttachmentInfo (which records the SHA256 of attachments processed by Defender for Office 365) with DeviceFileEvents (which records the SHA256 of files seen/executed on endpoints via Defender for Endpoint) on the shared SHA256 column, then projecting DeviceName/DeviceId for matching rows. This SHA256-based join is the standard way to pivot from an email-borne threat to the endpoints where that file actually landed. The specific hotspot selections remain as originally recorded since they were only shown in an image."
