    "id": "ed-44-596f7520",
    "number": 55,
    "topic": "Perform threat hunting",
    "type": "hotspot",
    "text": "You have a Microsoft 365 E5 subscription.\nYou need to create a hunting query that will return every email that contains an attachment named Document.pdf. The query must meet the following requirements:\n-Only show emails sent during the last hour.\n-Optimize query performance.\nHow should you complete the query? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNote: Each correct selection is worth one point.\nHot Area:",
    "images": [
      "https://www.exam-dumps.net/images/exams/SC-200/caa39d92-e221-4d21-b78c-b3f0a900a2fc.jpg"
    ],
    "choices": [],
    "correctLetters": [],
    "answerImage": "https://www.exam-dumps.net/images/exams/SC-200/12c8850a-5aa3-43a6-bccc-de0297a3a642.jpg",
    "explanation": "La requête doit rechercher dans la table EmailAttachmentInfo (ou EmailEvents jointe à EmailAttachmentInfo) les lignes où FileName == \"Document.pdf\", et pour des raisons de performance, le filtre temporel (where Timestamp > ago(1h)) doit être appliqué le plus tôt possible dans la requête, afin qu'Advanced Hunting/KQL puisse élaguer les données avant d'évaluer le filtre textuel, plus coûteux. Placer en premier les filtres larges et indexés comme la plage temporelle est le modèle d'optimisation des performances KQL standard, utilisé dans l'ensemble de la documentation de chasse aux menaces de Microsoft Defender XDR.",
    "referenceUrl": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-xdr/advanced-hunting-best-practices",
    "interactive": {
      "kind": "select-blanks",
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "EmailAttachmentInfo\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "blank",
          "id": "b1",
          "options": [
            "| join DeviceFileEvents on SHA256",
            "| join kind=inner (DeviceFileEvents | where Timestamp > ago(1h)) on SHA256",
            "| where Timestamp > ago(1h)",
            "| where Timestamp < ago(1h)"
          ],
          "correct": "| where Timestamp > ago(1h)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "\n| where Subject == \"Document Attachment\" and FileName == \"Document.pdf\"\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "blank",
          "id": "b2",
          "options": [
            "| join DeviceFileEvents on SHA256",
            "| join kind=inner (DeviceFileEvents | where Timestamp > ago(1h)) on SHA256",
            "| where Timestamp > ago(1h)",
            "| where Timestamp < ago(1h)"
          ],
          "correct": "| join kind=inner (DeviceFileEvents | where Timestamp > ago(1h)) on SHA256"
        }
      ]
    },
    "text_fr": "Vous disposez d'un abonnement Microsoft 365 E5.\nVous devez créer une requête de hunting qui renverra tous les e-mails contenant une pièce jointe nommée Document.pdf. La requête doit répondre aux exigences suivantes :\n-Afficher uniquement les e-mails envoyés au cours de la dernière heure.\n-Optimiser les performances de la requête.\nComment devez-vous compléter la requête ? Pour répondre, sélectionnez les options appropriées dans la zone de réponse.\nRemarque : chaque sélection correcte vaut un point.\nHot Area:",
    "explanation_en": "The query needs to search the EmailAttachmentInfo (or EmailEvents joined with EmailAttachmentInfo) table for FileName == \"Document.pdf\", and for performance it must apply the time filter (where Timestamp > ago(1h)) as early as possible in the query so Advanced Hunting/KQL can prune data before evaluating the more expensive string filter. Placing broad, indexed filters like time range first is the standard KQL performance optimization pattern used throughout Microsoft Defender XDR hunting guidance."
