    "text_fr": "Vous créez un abonnement Azure nommé sub1.\nDans sub1, vous créez un espace de travail Log Analytics nommé workspace1.\nVous activez Microsoft Defender for Cloud et configurez Defender for Cloud pour utiliser workspace1.\nVous devez collecter les journaux d'événements de sécurité des machines virtuelles Azure qui envoient leurs données à workspace1.\nQue devez-vous faire ?",
    "explanation_en": "In Microsoft Defender for Cloud (classic Log Analytics agent-based experience), raw Windows security event logs are stored in the connected Log Analytics workspace only if you explicitly turn on the Data collection setting (choosing a tier such as Common, Minimal, or All Events) from Defender for Cloud's Pricing & settings / Environment settings. The Log Analytics agent itself still evaluates security events for threat detection regardless of this setting, but storing/collecting the raw events for search and investigation in workspace1 requires enabling data collection. Registering a resource provider, creating a workbook, or configuring workflow automation do not control whether security events are ingested into the workspace."
