    "explanation_en": "A Microsoft Sentinel playbook is an Azure Logic Apps workflow triggered by an automation rule that can call out to external systems, such as opening a ticket in a service-management platform and posting a message to a Teams or Slack channel, which matches Microsoft's documented 'bi-directional sync' and 'orchestration' playbook use cases. A workbook only visualizes data, a hunting query only searches data, and a Defender XDR device group is just a grouping construct for applying policies to devices, none of which can call external APIs or post to chat platforms."
