    "explanation_en": "Microsoft Defender XDR automatically correlates related alerts across email, identity, and endpoint signals into a single incident, and the attack story graph then visualizes how the affected user, mailbox, device, and alerts relate chronologically as one attack chain. Together these two capabilities let an analyst see the phishing, compromised-account, and endpoint alerts as one coherent multi-stage attack rather than three unrelated events. A Purview retention label (C) is a compliance control with no bearing on alert correlation, a Secure Score recommendation (D) is a posture metric, and filtering completed remediation actions (E) only shows past actions already taken."
