    "explanation_en": "Microsoft Sentinel graph is a relationship-first analytics capability, built on the Sentinel data lake, that lets hunters traverse and visually explore multi-hop connections between entities such as accounts, IP addresses, cloud resources, and devices instead of reviewing each as an isolated table row. This graph-based exploration surfaces blast radius and hidden pivots that are hard to see in flat log data. A data collection rule (B) only governs ingestion, email notifications (C) are an alerting mechanism, and an eDiscovery export (D) is a compliance/legal-hold tool — none provide entity-relationship visualization."
