    "explanation_en": "A let statement binds a name to a scalar value, tabular expression, or function so it can be referenced repeatedly later in the same query, which is exactly what's needed to define a suspicious-IP list once and reuse it. The project operator only selects/renames columns in the current pipeline, distinct removes duplicate rows, and render is purely for visualizing results - none of them create a reusable named definition."
