    "explanation_en": "Microsoft Sentinel requires a mandatory closing classification (such as True Positive, Benign Positive, or one of the False Positive reasons) whenever an incident's status is set to Closed, so the reason for closing is always captured for later reporting and tuning. This classification step is separate from, and doesn't require, creating new analytics rules, recording a Graph application ID, or downloading an investigation package. The requirement exists specifically to stop incidents from being closed without a documented justification."
