    "explanation_en": "The Sensitive tag (sensitive group) identifies high-value accounts or groups that require stronger protection (for example, to detect lateral movement paths leading to them); it does not turn an account into a honeytoken lure. To configure accounts meant to be exploited by attackers, the Honeytoken tag must be applied directly to the accounts themselves, not by marking their group as Sensitive. The goal is therefore not achieved."
